WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.800
There are a lot of artists
and companies around the world

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.740
that build big moving structures for art.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.420
There are plenty of stage shows,
theme park attractions, and arena tours,

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.600
which need massive mechanical stuff
to move around.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.670
Here in Nantes,
in the west of France, though,

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:17.170
there's one place
that builds things slightly differently.

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:19.940
Les Machines de l'île,
the island machines,

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.260
are best known
for their giant mechanical elephant.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.620
12 meters high, weighing 48 tons,

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.650
it regularly "goes for a walk"
around the city.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:31.520
But the big difference here is:
this offers rides to tourists.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.000
Unlike a lot of theme park attractions,

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.730
not only does the elephant
have to put on four shows a day,

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:40.530
it has to put on those shows safely
with people of all ages on board.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:44.520
The two creators started this
because... they could!

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.830
There was a desire from the mayor

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:52.050
to renovate all this place
and the project fitted very well.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:56.260
The elephant was constructed
at first in 2004,

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:58.540
from 2004 to 2007,

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.920
about 30 months of construction.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:04.320
All the machine that have been made
for the project of Les machines de l'île

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.550
used wood, stainless steel, and leather,
mainly these three.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:12.720
We use plastic on some parts,
but very few,

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.250
because we don't want to use plastic
as much as we can.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.660
We have hybrid motorization

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.300
that will power the elephant
through the two back wheels.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.670
For the legs of the elephants,

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:25.970
many people think
that they're making it walk,

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:29.900
but if they touch the ground,
they do not push him forward.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.950
The elephant works as an automaton.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:37.160
For the movement of the head or the ears,
the eyes, and also the trunk,

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.780
they are all programmed in a computer.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.740
You have 44 hydraulic cylinders
on the machine,

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.150
6 gas cylinders,
and finally, 4 pneumatic cylinders.

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:50.810
To make the elephant move,
we need at least two people,

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.890
one pilot, and one guide
inside the elephant

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:57.020
to assure the safety of people inside,

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:00.020
but also to make
the scream of the elephant.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:04.540
We may have about
200, 300 people around the elephant

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.300
moving with him during his walk,

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:11.500
but we always keep a security perimeter
of about five-meter distance

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.760
between the front wheel and the crowd.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.240
The elephant is about 48 tons,

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:23.580
so it could be very risky
for anyone to get under a leg.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:26.670
Safety here makes a lot more sense
when you get close up.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:29.500
Yes, there are a lot of moving parts,
particularly, in the middle.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.880
We're not allowed to film,
but you don't get close to them.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.160
The same way if you're riding on a bus,

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:35.380
you can't actually get close
to the engine or the wheels.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:38.480
Ultimately, this is a slow
and weirdly shaped bus.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.890
You can stand up on a bus or a train
going 50, 100 times the speed

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:44.050
with much sharper
acceleration and braking.

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:47.080
Now there are places that would've made
getting on board an exclusive experience,

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.290
and honestly,
if I was in charge of a show like this,

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.501
I'd be tempted to say that...

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:51.367
[elephant screams]

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:53.230
yes, maybe a few people can ride,

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:57.340
but we'll charge them €100 each
and it's restricted only to VIPs.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.680
[elephant continues screaming]
That way... [laughs]

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.970
That way, it's much less of a hassle.
[scream ends]

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.790
But a ride on this elephant
is less than €10.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:06.030
They have a boarding procedure
like an airport

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.730
and there are 50 passengers
allowed on board.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.830
The most impressive part
of this whole thing for me

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:14.500
is not that it works.
It's that it works to theme park standards

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.210
show after show, day after day,
year after year

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:20.080
in the real world with people on board,

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.590
and it's not the only attraction here.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:26.010
This place is the older warehouse,

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:28.810
the old workshop
of the division shipyards.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.760
Inside the gallery,
we have a lot of machines.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:35.340
We have a caterpillar, we have a heron,
we have a spider, all giant machines.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.280
We have also smaller machines.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.790
During the visit,
we take randomly a visitor

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:42.440
to take part on a trip on the machine,

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:46.100
or to move several parts of the machine
during the presentation.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:50.240
Every machinist needs training
of about one month and a half

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.580
to move every machine inside the gallery.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:57.810
The most difficult to move is the spider,
because it works as an excavator.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:01.220
It's very complicated, as you move
two diggers at the same time.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.590
After the spider,

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:06.610
the other most complicated machine
should be the little heron.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:07.950
"Little" is a euphemism,

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:12.460
because it's about 7.5 meters wingspan

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.170
and about 3 meters high.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:17.800
We have a lot of parts to move,
especially the wings.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:22.040
The Sea World carousel
is a carousel about 25 meters high.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:26.610
Inside you find 36 machines,
where you can go inside and take a turn.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:32.980
The machines are inspired
of fantastic worlds or real sea fish.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:35.280
- A lot of workshops
and art projects like this

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:36.440
can struggle to pay the rent.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.430
Charging people for rides and admission

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:41.520
is a great way
to make big art like this sustainable.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:44.410
Between the elephant,
the gallery, and the carousel,

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:46.930
this is basically a small theme park now,

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.930
but more than that, it's affected
the reputation of the whole town.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:52.320
Some of the funding
for building that elephant and all of this

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:53.720
came from local government

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:56.260
as part of a deliberate attempt
to change the city's image

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.670
and make it somewhere
more appealing to tourists.

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:01.540
The question, "why would you
want to visit Nantes?"

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:04.660
now has an answer:
because there's nowhere else

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:09.060
you can ride a giant mechanical elephant
and still have change from €10.

